  "live_records": {
    "q-184102": {
      "dom_id": "step-q184102",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Suppose $n=10m+4,$ where $m\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument showing that $n$ is even.\n\nThe number $n$ is even since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =10m+4 \\\\  & =2({{field-1}}) \\\\  & ={{field-2}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have defined $a=$ {{field-3}}, which is an integer.",
      "worked_solution": "An integer is *even* if it can be written as $2a,$ where $a$ is an integer.\n\nTherefore, we complete our argument as follows:\n\nThe number $n$ is even since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =10m+4 \\\\  & =2({{5m+2}_{⏟}}_{a}) \\\\  & =2a,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we have defined $a=5m+2,$ which is an integer.",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
