    "q-184062": {
      "dom_id": "step-q184062",
      "name": "Question 8",
      "problem": "Suppose $n=4i+2j-8,$ where $i,j\\in Z.$ Complete the following argument.\n\nThe number $n$ is {{field-1}} since \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =4i+2j-8 \\\\  & =2({{field-2}}-4) \\\\  & ={{field-3}},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a=${{field-4}}.",
      "worked_solution": "An integer is *even* if it can be written as $2a,$ where $a$ is an integer.\n\nNotice that all terms in the expression $4i+2j-8$ have a common factor of $2.$ \n\nTherefore, we complete our argument as follows:\n\nThe number $n$ is $\\text{even}$ since\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =4i+2j-8 \\\\  & =2({{2i+j-4}_{⏟}}_{a}) \\\\  & =2a,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $a=2i+j-4\\in Z.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
